multi("m1-b05", S4,
 "A parts catalog index on a standard Vector Search endpoint returns poor results when engineers type exact part codes such as HX-4471 mixed with plain descriptions. Results must also be limited to the engineer's region, stored in a region column. Which two changes to the similarity_search call meet both needs?",
 ["Set query_type to hybrid so keyword matches on part codes combine with vector similarity",
  "Pass filters={\"region\": [\"EU\"]} so only rows for the engineer's region are returned",
  "Pass filters='region = \"EU\"' as a SQL-like string so only that region's rows return",
  "Add a reranker so the top results are reordered by relevance after vector retrieval",
  "Raise num_results to 500 so the exact part code is more likely to appear in results"],
 [0, 1], 2, "the SQL-like string is the filter syntax for storage-optimized endpoints; a standard endpoint takes a dictionary.",
 T("That a better ranker fixes exact-token misses. Embeddings blur codes like HX-4471; hybrid search adds keyword matching. Filter syntax depends on the endpoint type.",
   [["Exact codes or rare tokens missed", "Retrieval method", "query_type hybrid (vector plus keyword)"],
    ["Restrict by a metadata column, standard endpoint", "Filter syntax", "Dictionary filters"],
    ["Restrict by a column, storage-optimized endpoint", "Filter syntax", "SQL-like string filters"]],
   [["\"exact part codes such as HX-4471\"", "Keyword matching needed: hybrid."], ["\"on a standard Vector Search endpoint\"", "Dictionary filter syntax."]],
   "Codes and IDs: hybrid search. Standard endpoints filter with a dictionary; storage-optimized ones with a SQL-like string.",
   "Create and query a Vector Search index"),
 "Search the library by the exact catalogue number and by topic at once, and only on your own floor.",
 D + "vector-search/query-vector-search",
 why=["Correct: hybrid search combines keyword and vector results, so exact part codes are matched.",
      "Correct: standard endpoints take filters as a dictionary of column to allowed values.",
      "Wrong: the SQL-like string format is for storage-optimized endpoints, not standard ones.",
      "Wrong: a reranker reorders what retrieval returned; if the exact code was never retrieved, reordering can't add it.",
      "Wrong: more results add noise and cost and still rely on vector similarity, which is what misses the codes."]),

